---
/* =============================================================================
   The homepage — one implementation, two languages
   =============================================================================
   Both `/` and `/ar/` render this. The alternative — two 300-line page files —
   guarantees they drift apart, and a drifted Arabic homepage is exactly the
   "visual afterthought" §10 forbids.

   ── THE ORDER ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

     1. Hero                          I ❤ Tech
     2. What I'm Exploring Now        Building · Testing · Learning
     3. Vibe Coding                   building with AI
     4. Latest                        real published content, or nothing
     5. Gear                          using and testing technology
     6. Learn                         the gateway to the library
     7. About + Newsletter            the close
     8. Footer                        (Base.astro)

   §2 answers the question a first-time visitor actually arrives with — "what
   is this person doing right now" — before the page starts arguing for
   individual pillars. Three doors, named, one screen.

   ── TWO PHASE 1 CHANGES TO THE v2 ORDER ─────────────────────────────────────
   The Playground section is gone from this page. It is PARKED, not deleted —
   `parked.playground` in site.config.ts, which is also what takes it out of the
   header, the footer and the Learn Hub. /playground still resolves.

   Latest has moved UP, from below Learn to directly under Vibe Coding. Its old
   position was reasoned from the v2 IA: a feed is the least opinionated thing
   on the page, so it sat after everything the reader could DO. Phase 1 inverts
   that premise — the whole point of this phase is that newly published work is
   the most important thing on the site, and a feed that appears sixth is a feed
   nobody scrolls to. The personal close is still last.

   ── EVERY SECTION COLLAPSES ON ITS OWN ──────────────────────────────────────
   §3 and §5 are gated on real assets (a build needs a real screenshot, a gear
   story needs a real photograph), §4 disappears below two items, §6 drops any
   surface with nothing published. §2 never collapses — it is navigation, and
   all three destinations have designed empty states of their own.

   With an empty content directory this page is a hero, three doors, four honest
   lines and a close — which is the correct state, not a broken one.

   CS-05: exactly one primary action on this page, and it is the hero's. Every
   other action below is secondary, ghost or a plain link.
   ========================================================================== */

import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Hero from '../home/Hero.astro';
import Exploring from '../home/Exploring.astro';
import RealWorld from '../home/RealWorld.astro';
import GearSection from '../home/GearSection.astro';
import LearnSection from '../home/LearnSection.astro';
import Latest from '../home/Latest.astro';
import AboutSubscribe from '../home/AboutSubscribe.astro';
import { site } from '../../site.config';
import type { Lang } from '../../i18n';

interface Props {
  lang: Lang;
}

const { lang } = Astro.props;

const description = lang === 'ar' ? site.descriptionAr : site.description;
---

<Base lang={lang} padded={false} description={description}>
  {/* 1 — Hero. I ❤ Tech. */}
  <Hero lang={lang} />

  {/* 2 — What I'm exploring now. Three doors: Building, Testing, Learning. */}
  <Exploring lang={lang} />

  {/* 3 — Vibe Coding in the Real World. Building with AI. */}
  <RealWorld lang={lang} />

  {/* 4 — Latest. Real published content, or nothing at all. */}
  <Latest lang={lang} />

  {/* 5 — Gear. Using and testing technology. */}
  <GearSection lang={lang} />

  {/* 6 — Learn. The gateway to the library, not the library. */}
  <LearnSection lang={lang} />

  {/* 7 — About + Subscribe. The close. */}
  <AboutSubscribe lang={lang} />

  {/* 8 — Footer, from Base.astro. */}
</Base>
